Here's an example of how to generate an automatic table of contents in LaTeX:

## Basic Example

```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}

\title{My Document}
\author{Your Name}
\date{\today}

\begin{document}

\maketitle

% Generate the table of contents
\tableofcontents
\newpage  % Optional: start content on new page

\section{Introduction}
This is the introduction section.

\section{Literature Review}
This section covers the literature review.

\subsection{Previous Studies}
Information about previous studies.

\subsection{Research Gaps}
Discussion of research gaps.

\section{Methodology}
This section describes the methodology.

\subsection{Data Collection}
How data was collected.

\subsection{Analysis Methods}
Methods used for analysis.

\section{Results}
This section presents the results.

\section{Conclusion}
Final thoughts and conclusions.

\end{document}
```

## Enhanced Example with Customization

```latex
\documentclass{report}
\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}
\usepackage{tocloft}  % For customizing TOC appearance

\title{Advanced Document}
\author{Your Name}
\date{\today}

% Customize TOC appearance
\renewcommand{\cftsecleader}{\cftdotfill{\cftdotsep}}  % Add dots for sections
\setcounter{tocdepth}{3}  % Show up to subsubsections in TOC

\begin{document}

\maketitle

% Generate table of contents
\tableofcontents
\listoffigures   % Optional: list of figures
\listoftables    % Optional: list of tables
\clearpage

\chapter{First Chapter}
Content of the first chapter.

\section{First Section}
Section content.

\subsection{Subsection}
Subsection content.

\subsubsection{Subsubsection}
Subsubsection content.

\chapter{Second Chapter}
Content of the second chapter.

\section{Another Section}
More content here.

\end{document}
```

## Key Commands Explained

- **`\tableofcontents`**: Generates the table of contents automatically
- **`\listoffigures`**: Creates a list of figures (if you have figures)
- **`\listoftables`**: Creates a list of tables (if you have tables)
- **`\setcounter{tocdepth}{n}`**: Controls depth of TOC (0=chapters only, 1=sections, 2=subsections, 3=subsubsections)
- **`\newpage` or `\clearpage`**: Forces a page break after TOC

## Important Notes

1. **Compile twice**: You need to compile your LaTeX document twice for the TOC to appear correctly (first run generates the .toc file, second run includes it).

2. **Automatic updates**: The TOC updates automatically when you add, remove, or rename sections.

3. **Page numbers**: Page numbers in the TOC are generated automatically and update when content changes.

4. **Hyperlinks**: Add `\usepackage{hyperref}` to make TOC entries clickable links to their respective sections.

The table of contents will automatically include all `\chapter`, `\section`, `\subsection`, and `\subsubsection` commands with their corresponding page numbers.

